264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A limiting amplifier is a key component in intermediate frequency \(IF\) and radio frequency \(RF\) communication systems. Its primary function is to amplify weak signals while suppressing strong signal variations, ensuring a constant output amplitude despite input level fluctuations. This makes it particularly useful in applications such as wireless receivers, FM demodulation, and radar systems.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Working Principle:)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( A limiting amplifier consists of multiple gain stages, each amplifying the signal while progressively reducing the variations in amplitude. At a certain threshold, further increases in input power do not affect the output amplitude, resulting in a "clipped" or limited output signal.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
